## 1. Reverse string function

`src/reverseString.ts`:

```typescript
/**
 * Reverses a string, preserving Unicode code points (e.g. emoji).
 */
export function reverseString(input: string): string {
  return [...input].reverse().join("");
}
```

Why this approach:

- `[...input]` splits by Unicode code points, so surrogate pairs (emoji, etc.) stay intact.
- `.split("").reverse().join("")` can break multi-byte characters.
- Empty string returns `""`.

